+PR 2 cannot begin against an implied or prose-only interface. Its entry gate requires one landed, versioned audio/upload contract at a recorded `origin/main` SHA. That contract must fix the supported codec/container, sample format and rate, channel count/layout and `source_kind`, chunk duration/range, and the authenticated create/upload/status/delete routes. Create binds the capture to the server-derived actor and immutable consent evidence. Upload binds `(capture_session_id, sequence, digest)` to that actor/session. Status returns the durable contiguous acknowledgement boundary plus any explicit gaps; delete is actor-bound and idempotent. An acknowledgement is valid only when the returned session, sequence, and digest match. Missing or incompatible fields stop DEV; the desktop lane must not guess defaults or add a private endpoint.
