 ## Architecture
@@ -76,18 +78,21 @@ The Tauri webview renders a small control/status surface. All privileged work—
 
 ### Native audio choice
 
-Windows system audio uses WASAPI loopback through the `windows` crate and COM, not a browser API or a generic abstraction that cannot prove loopback semantics. Capture the default render endpoint in shared mode; observe endpoint changes and recover without reusing stale handles. Microphone and system frames carry monotonic timestamps and distinct `source_kind` values. Do not claim speaker identity from mixed system audio.
+Windows system audio uses whole-system WASAPI loopback through the `windows` crate and COM, not a browser API or a generic abstraction that cannot prove loopback semantics. Capture the default render endpoint in shared mode; observe endpoint changes and recover without reusing stale handles. This intentionally records every sound routed to that endpoint, including notifications, music, and unrelated applications. Preflight and recording UI must say so plainly; tests inject unrelated notification/program audio and prove it is retained as system-source evidence without false attribution. Process-specific application loopback is deferred to Forge issue `701a8a03-f924-4167-9172-6022903ec93d` and must not enter the MVP as an undocumented filter or fallback. Microphone and system frames carry monotonic timestamps and distinct `source_kind` values. Do not claim speaker identity from mixed system audio.
 
-macOS system audio uses Core Audio Process Tap on macOS 14.2+. Apple documents audio taps as an audio-only way to capture outgoing audio from processes or process groups, with an OS permission prompt and `NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription`. It is a closer least-privilege match than ScreenCaptureKit, whose screen-capture permission and visual stream surface are unnecessary for this recorder. PR 1 has a blocking physical-device spike on Intel and Apple Silicon for permission first-run/denial/revocation, aggregate device creation, device changes, sleep/wake, silence, one-hour stability, and simultaneous mic capture. If that spike cannot meet the gate, stop and return to PLAN for a bounded ScreenCaptureKit alternative; do not silently add it as a fallback. Pre-14.2 macOS is outside MVP for the same reason.
+macOS system audio uses Core Audio Process Tap on macOS 14.2+. Apple documents audio taps as an audio-only way to capture outgoing audio from processes or process groups, with an OS permission prompt and `NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription`. It is a closer least-privilege match than ScreenCaptureKit, whose screen-capture permission and visual stream surface are unnecessary for this recorder. PR 1 begins with a bounded native spike and ends at a terminal decision gate on physical Intel and Apple Silicon hardware: either permission first-run/denial/revocation, aggregate device creation, device changes, sleep/wake, silence, one-hour stability, and simultaneous mic capture all pass and implementation continues, or PR 1 stops and PLAN is amended with the captured evidence before a bounded ScreenCaptureKit spike. Do not silently add or ship a fallback. Pre-14.2 macOS is outside MVP for the same reason.
 
 Capture keeps mic and system audio as separately identified tracks/channels through the upload contract when the landed durability API supports it. If the landed API only accepts one audio body, the upstream contract must first add an explicit topology-preserving representation. The desktop app must not locally collapse sources, infer speakers, or add an undocumented multiplexing format.
 
+MVP performs no acoustic echo cancellation, noise suppression, voice isolation, or content-dependent muting. Digital system loopback and microphone stay separate so downstream evidence can represent uncertainty. Headphones are the recommended setup: preflight explains that speakers can leak remote/system audio into the mic track and create duplicate speech. Physical gates cover wired/Bluetooth headset and open-speaker scenarios, measure cross-track leakage, clipping, drift, and feedback, and prove the collector preserves both sources and labels the acoustic limitation rather than dropping audio. Adding AEC is a new DSP/privacy contract and returns to PLAN.
+
 ### Collector state machine
 
 Allowed states are `signed_out`, `permission_required`, `ready`, `recording`, `paused`, `stopping`, `draining`, `complete`, `recoverable`, `discarding`, and `error`.
 
 - Only a foreground `Start` action may transition `ready -> recording`.
-- A calendar suggestion may populate a proposed association but cannot invoke capture or a privileged Tauri command.
+- Product-Suite authentication and server actor binding are required before `ready`. A calendar or existing-meeting association is not required.
+- A calendar suggestion may populate a proposed association but cannot invoke capture or a privileged Tauri command. Starting without an association asks the server to create an opaque actor-bound capture session/meeting and returns only its identifier to the collector.
 - Every chunk transitions `captured -> encrypted_and_fsynced -> upload_eligible -> in_flight -> acknowledged -> deleted`.
 - Failed, timed-out, 429, or 5xx uploads return to `upload_eligible` with bounded exponential backoff and full jitter; honor `Retry-After` and cap concurrency.
 - 401/403, tenant mismatch, invalid acknowledgement, sequence/digest conflict, invalid TLS, missing key, spool corruption, or updater-signature failure is fail-closed. Preserve recoverable ciphertext and show a blocking status; never mark acknowledged or finalize.
@@ -101,13 +106,13 @@ Use an application-private directory and an encrypted, versioned per-session man
 
 Write ciphertext and manifest updates to a same-directory temporary file, flush file contents, atomically rename, and flush the parent directory where supported before upload eligibility. Set owner-only permissions/ACLs. Enforce a configurable bounded quota (initial gate: 2 GiB or 8 hours, whichever comes first), surface low disk space before start, and pause capture before data becomes unspoolable. Delete only after validating the authenticated acknowledgement matches session, sequence, and digest.
 
