+Desktop login uses the existing Product-Suite browser-based authentication flow and an app-owned deep link with PKCE/state/nonce. Authentication is mandatory for session creation, upload, status, delete, and finalization even when no calendar or existing-meeting association is chosen. The Rust layer exchanges the one-time result and stores the opaque refresh/session credential in the OS credential store; the webview receives only authentication state. A callback mismatch, expired state, or missing secure store fails closed. Signing and updater private keys exist only in protected release CI, never in the repository or desktop runtime.
 
 ### Consent, permissions, and association
 
-The first screen explains mic/system capture, Product-Suite upload, local encrypted recovery, retention/deletion, and the always-visible recording indicator. Preflight tests both sources and shows separate level meters. Start is disabled until the OS permissions are granted and the current Product-Suite actor/meeting authority is confirmed. During recording, both the compact window and tray/menu-bar item display a persistent red indicator, duration, pause, and stop; closing the window does not obscure the tray indicator or stop recording without confirmation.
+The first screen explains mic/system capture, whole-system contamination on Windows, Product-Suite upload, local encrypted recovery, retention/deletion, headset/AEC limitations, and the always-visible recording indicator. Preflight tests both sources and shows separate level meters. Start is disabled until OS permissions and Product-Suite authentication are valid and the server accepts immutable consent evidence containing the server-derived actor, server time, requested capture sources, consent-policy version, and UI locale. The same evidence is bound to the capture session and authenticated chunk metadata; retries cannot mutate it. Missing, stale-policy, actor-mismatched, or incomplete consent is rejected before audio capture. During recording, both the compact window and tray/menu-bar item display a persistent red indicator, duration, pause, and stop; closing the window does not obscure the tray indicator or stop recording without confirmation.
 
-Calendar association is optional and read-only. The app requests backend-provided suggestions and displays title/time/organizer minimally. A user confirms one event or chooses no event. The collector submits only the selected opaque association identifier alongside the existing meeting/session request. It stores no calendar credential and never starts, schedules, or resumes a recording from an event.
+Calendar or existing-meeting association is optional and read-only. The app requests backend-provided suggestions and displays title/time/organizer minimally. A user confirms one event, selects an existing meeting, or chooses no association. With no association, the authenticated create route creates an opaque server capture session/meeting; local data does not supply a title, tenant, owner, or authority. The collector submits only a user-confirmed opaque association identifier when present. It stores no calendar credential and never starts, schedules, or resumes a recording from an event.
 
